  "prefLabel": "Cul-H 102.42 State archaeologist",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Cul-H 102.42 “State archaeologist” means the archaeologist in the division designated by the director with the approval of the commissioner to develop, supervise and coordinate activities necessary to discharge and integrate the powers and duties of the division in the field of archeology as mandated by federal and state laws and procedures.\n\nSource. #10217, eff 10-30-12, EXPIRED: 7-1-18",
